                  <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                  <msItem>
                     <title>Turgotus, Vita s. Margarete, etc.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">John Durkan, letter 10. 2. 1969, gives contents
                        as:</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Margaret; Jocelin of Furness, Waldef; [Thomas
                        Hibernicus,] De tribus punctis christiane religionis; Thomas Hibernicus, "De
                        confessione"; De gaudiis paradisi; Augustine, De miseria hominis; Speculum
                        claustralium; De contemptu mundi; Bernard (as in Opera 5. 421 = Walter Map,
                        147); Disputacio inter corpus et animam (Map, 95); Excerpts from Hugh of St.
                        Victor and other works; Treatise on prayer, "Quidam clericus in nimia
                        tristitia, dententus [recte: detentus] et conquerens ...".</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Cf. J. Durkan, "Three Manuscripts with Fife
                        associations", Innes Review 20 (1969) 47–49 &amp; pl. xvii (which shows
                        fol. 1r).</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
